Package: datamysteries
Title: Data Mystery Cases for Learning R and the Tidyverse
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Hugo",
        family = "Cornejo Villena",
        email = "hcornejovillena@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Author: Hugo Cornejo Villena [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Hugo Cornejo Villena <hcornejovillena@gmail.com>
Description: A collection of fictional data "mysteries" for teaching R
    and the tidyverse through case-based learning. Each case presents a
    narrative applied problem that students investigate with progressively
    introduced R/tidyverse commands, ruling out decoy hypotheses to
    uncover an evidence-based explanation. Cases can cover business,
    fraud, operations, environmental, health, engineering, education, or
    other applied domains. Datasets and narratives are provided
    bilingually (Spanish/English) when available.
